3) A balloon is in the form of right circular cylindrical of radius 1.5m and length 4m and is Surmounted by hemispherical end. If the radius is increased by 0.01 m and length by 0.05m, find the  percentage change in volume of balloon.

syms r h dr dh;
V = pi * r^2 * h + (2/3) * pi * r^3;
dV = diff(V, r) * dr + diff(V, h) * dh;
r_val = 1.5; % meters
h_val = 4;   % meters
dr_val = 0.01; % meters
dh_val = 0.05; % meters
V_value = double(subs(V, {r, h}, {r_val, h_val}));
dV_value = double(subs(dV, {r, h, dr, dh}, {r_val, h_val, dr_val, dh_val}));
percentage_change = (dV_value / V_value) * 100

Output

