4) Divide 24 into 3 parts such that the continued product of the first, square of the second and the cube of the third may be maximum.

syms x y z lambda
L = x * y^2 * z^3 + lambda * (24 - x - y - z);
eq1 = diff(L, x) == 0; eq2 = diff(L, y) == 0; 
eq3 = diff(L, z) == 0; eq4 = diff(L, lambda) == 0;
sol = solve([eq1, eq2, eq3, eq4], [x, y, z, lambda], 'Real', true);
x_vals = double(sol.x); y_vals = double(sol.y); z_vals = double(sol.z);
for i = 1:length(x_vals)
    if x_vals(i) &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; y_vals(i) &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; z_vals(i) &gt; 0
        x_sol = x_vals(i)
        y_sol = y_vals(i)
        z_sol = z_vals(i)
        break;
    end
end
max_product = x_sol * y_sol^2 * z_sol^3

Output:
 
x_sol = 4
y_sol = 8
z_sol = 12
max_product = 442368

